    "summary": "Jam‑heavy Saint Stephen, Easy Wind, and intense Other One",
    "blurb": "The set delivers a soaring I Know You Rider acoustic moment and a jam‑rich Saint Stephen, while the second set erupts with an explosive The Other One and a rare Easy Wind/It's A Man’s World pairing. Jerry’s voice shines on Black Peter and Bob adds raw intensity during The Other One.",
    "review": "June 5 1970 at Fillmore West captures the Dead in a transitional phase, balancing folk‑rock intimacy with electric fire. The first set rolls smoothly from Dire Wolf into an acoustic gem of I Know You Rider, then builds momentum through Black Peter and New Speedway Boogie. The second set is where the night truly ignites: Easy Wind flows into the soulful It's A Man’s World, and the band launches into a sprawling Other One that feels both chaotic and purposeful – even Bob’s shouted “GODDAMMIT!” adds to the raw edge. The encore closes with Saint Stephen segueing into Casey Jones, leaving the audience buzzing. Across all sources, Garcia’s vocals are praised as crystal‑clear, especially on Black Peter, while the matrix recording by Bear/Wise captures the high‑energy dynamics and instrument separation better than any other tape of the night.",
